        "content": "<p>Awesome! This brings me back to 1983, when I first started coding in Basic on a <a href=\"https://js99er.net/#/\">TI-99/4a</a>! <span aria-label=\"smile\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f604\" role=\"img\" title=\"smile\">:smile:</span></p>",
        "id": 624518730,
        "sender_full_name": "Aurélien Geron",
        "timestamp": 1789529266
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"734214\">Aurélien Geron</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/304902-show-and-tell/topic/BASIC.20.281964.29.2C.20in.20Roc.20.282026.29/near/624518730\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Awesome! This brings me back to 1983, when I first started coding in Basic on a <a href=\"https://js99er.net/#/\">TI-99/4a</a>! <span aria-label=\"smile\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f604\" role=\"img\" title=\"smile\">:smile:</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>That was my first computer as well! Either 1982 or 1983. They had a PacMan clone called MunchMan. After I read their excellent tutorial, one of the first programs I wrote was a really bad version of MunchMan.</p>",
        "id": 624626410,
        "sender_full_name": "Steve Howell",
        "timestamp": 1789560692
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Haha, so cool, I used to love that game! You can play it now on the emulator I linked to (choose Software &gt; More... &gt; Search for MunchMan). <span aria-label=\"grinning face with smiling eyes\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f601\" role=\"img\" title=\"grinning face with smiling eyes\">:grinning_face_with_smiling_eyes:</span></p>",
